<TrustPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What the current Havemoon site stores, what browser tools process, and what must be updated before advertising or analytics are enabled."
  updated="August 12, 2026"
>
  <h2>Current preview status</h2>
  <p>
    This version of Havemoon is a static local preview. It does not currently run display
    advertising, behavioral analytics, user accounts, newsletter signup, or a server-side contact
    form.
  </p>

  <h2>Information processed in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators and checklists process entries in your browser for the current page session.
    They do not submit those values to Havemoon. Avoid entering confidential supplier, payment,
    personal, or regulated data.
  </p>

  <h2>Local storage</h2>
  <p>
    The site may store a theme preference in the browser so that light or dark mode remains
    consistent. Search is built from the site’s public static content.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
  <p>
    When a public host is selected, that provider may process ordinary request information such as
    IP address, user agent, requested URL, time, and security events. The final policy will identify
    the actual provider and retention practices before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising, consent, and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    No advertising service is active in this local preview. If Google advertising is enabled, Google
    and third-party vendors may use cookies, web beacons, IP addresses, or similar identifiers to
    serve and measure ads. Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies to serve ads based
    on a user's prior visits to this site or other sites. Users can review or change personalized
    advertising choices in
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or
    use the
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About Ads opt-out page</a
    >. The live policy must list any additional advertising vendors and their available opt-out
    methods before those vendors are enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent choices</h2>
  <p>
    Where advertising or analytics requires consent, the public site will show an appropriate notice
    before the relevant storage or processing begins. Users in the European Economic Area, the
    United Kingdom, or Switzerland may receive a Google-certified consent request when Google ads
    are served. The final consent mechanism, purposes, vendors, retention, and withdrawal method
    will be kept consistent with the actual production configuration and applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Google data-use information</h2>
  <p>
    For an explanation of how Google uses data when a visitor uses a partner site or app, see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Guides link to regulators and other primary sources. External websites operate under their own
    privacy policies; Havemoon does not control their collection practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact and data requests</h2>
  <p class="trust-note">
    The verified operator identity and public privacy contact will be inserted before the site is
    made public. This preview deliberately does not invent contact information.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
